v4.5.stable, v4.5.1.stable, v4.6.dev2, and later 4.5.dev snapshots\n- Not reproducible in v4.5.dev2.official [af2c71397], v4.4.stable, and earlier 4.5.dev snapshots\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.1.stable - macOS Sequoia (15.6.1) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M2 (Apple8) - Apple M2 (8 threads) - 16.00 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen the main window's scale factor is greater than 1, the window's title text and close button will be blurry. Notice how content within the window is clear, but the title and close button are blurry:\n\n<img width=\"273\" height=\"295\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d1e4f6f2-3bd6-47ed-aab3-5c8b06d84c31\" />\n\nNote that changing the `sampling_override` value on the embedded window does not effect the rendering of the window title.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a scene and add a Window node within\n2. In Project Settings, set `Display/Window/Stretch/Scale` to 2.0\n3. Optionally add a Label node with some text inside the embedded Window to see the difference in text rendering\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[embedded-window-title-test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23112323/embedded-window-title-test.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos